div.p:
The President returned to the question of steps to be taken. These included: 
                        a.

discuss the proposal with U Thant;
                        b.

discuss it with Adoula;
                        c.

if satisfactory conclusions arose from these discussions, put the
                            squadron in;
                        d.

reserve for a later time Congressional presentation;
                        e.

Bowles to include in his speech tonight our concern with the Communist threat in the Congo and the need to
                            protect the interests of both sides in the Congo-Katanga dispute;
                        f.

McGhee to do a backgrounder at the State Department explaining the
                            present state of the situation. He also was to approach Senator Dodd and
                            get whatever help from Senator Humphrey he could;
                        g.

George Ball was to look into the usefulness of bringing up to date and
                            issuing the Congo “White Paper,” which was drafted in the fall.
